WEBVTT

00:00:00.596 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.751 --> 00:00:05.950
In this lesson, we do a complete classic set, step by step:

00:00:06.141 --> 00:00:08.589
one extension on each natural lash.

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:11.310
Throughout the set, remember three things:

00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:15.397
the client's eyes stay closed, isolate exactly one lash,

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:17.550
and glue never touches the skin.

00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:19.002
Step one:

00:00:19.111 --> 00:00:20.042
consultation.

00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:24.362
Wash your hands, then sit and talk with the client while her eyes are still open.

00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:26.201
Ask about allergies:

00:00:26.454 --> 00:00:28.122
has she ever reacted to lash glue?

00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:29.802
Ask about her eyes:

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:34.682
are they red or itchy right now, any eye condition, any recent eye surgery?

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:38.602
If she wears contact lenses, ask her to take them out first.

00:00:38.985 --> 00:00:41.722
And ask what look she wants, natural or fuller.

00:00:41.953 --> 00:00:45.210
If there is a problem with her eyes, no service today,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.882
as in the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:00:48.556 --> 00:00:49.337
Step two:

00:00:49.745 --> 00:00:51.657
make the client really comfortable.

00:00:51.823 --> 00:00:56.297
A neck pillow, a light blanket, maybe a small pillow under the knees.

00:00:56.774 --> 00:01:01.994
A full classic set usually takes one and a half to two hours, and all that time,

00:01:01.944 --> 00:01:03.417
the client lies still,

00:01:03.446 --> 00:01:04.617
with her eyes closed.

00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:09.737
The more relaxed she is, the less her eyes move, and the more precise your work.

00:01:10.395 --> 00:01:11.181
Step three:

00:01:11.444 --> 00:01:13.021
cleanse the natural lashes.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.981
Oil, cream or eyeshadow left on the lashes makes the glue bond poorly.

00:01:18.314 --> 00:01:22.772
With lash cleanser and a soft brush, brush gently from the base to the tips,

00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:24.861
with the client's eyes still closed.

00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:29.332
Then rinse with clean water, and dry them thoroughly, with a small fan,

00:01:29.282 --> 00:01:30.461
or let them air dry.

00:01:31.143 --> 00:01:31.982
Step four:

00:01:32.243 --> 00:01:34.222
apply the gel under eye pads.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.566
The pad must fully cover all the lower lashes,

00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:40.622
so that no lower lash gets glued to the upper ones.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:44.372
The top edge of the pad sits right under the lower lash line,

00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:46.142
but does not touch the waterline,

00:01:46.324 --> 00:01:47.662
and does not touch the eye.

00:01:48.081 --> 00:01:51.055
If it does, the client feels scratchiness and stinging,

00:01:51.005 --> 00:01:53.342
and her eyes are red after the appointment.

00:01:53.575 --> 00:01:57.822
If any lower lash still pokes out, add a small piece of medical paper tape.

00:01:58.475 --> 00:01:59.418
Step five:

00:01:59.671 --> 00:02:02.578
brush the lashes with a disposable lash wand,

00:02:02.528 --> 00:02:05.498
so the natural lashes separate and lie evenly.

00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:08.058
Now look closely at the natural lashes:

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:12.698
which ones are healthy and long, which ones are young, short and fine.

00:02:13.127 --> 00:02:16.538
From that, choose the length and thickness for each zone.

00:02:17.213 --> 00:02:18.154
Step six:

00:02:18.252 --> 00:02:19.434
set up your station.

00:02:19.817 --> 00:02:21.994
A lash tray, arranged by length.

00:02:22.263 --> 00:02:25.914
A jade stone, or a glue ring, with a fresh drop of glue.

00:02:26.343 --> 00:02:27.274
And your tweezers:

00:02:27.623 --> 00:02:31.434
a straight one for isolating, and a curved one for picking up the lash.

00:02:31.863 --> 00:02:35.354
A lash wand and small cotton swabs, all disposable.

00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:38.554
The glue bottle, capped straight after you take the glue.

00:02:39.218 --> 00:02:40.075
Step seven:

00:02:40.418 --> 00:02:41.275
isolation.

00:02:41.814 --> 00:02:44.715
Your non dominant hand holds the straight tweezers.

00:02:45.061 --> 00:02:47.985
Slide them into the lashes, open the tips slightly,

00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:50.635
and push the neighboring lashes to either side,

00:02:50.745 --> 00:02:53.275
so that a single natural lash stands alone.

00:02:53.704 --> 00:02:54.795
Isolate it cleanly.

00:02:55.068 --> 00:02:58.715
Just one extra lash in there, and the glue will stick the two together.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.087
Step eight:

00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:02.887
pick up the extension and dip it in the glue.

00:03:03.296 --> 00:03:05.959
Your dominant hand holds the curved tweezers,

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:10.487
and picks up an extension near its base, where the lash is thick and straight.

00:03:10.742 --> 00:03:15.609
Then dip only the base of the extension into the glue drop, about 1–2 mm,

00:03:15.559 --> 00:03:17.127
and draw it out gently.

00:03:17.388 --> 00:03:21.527
Just enough glue, thin and even, no blob at the base.

00:03:22.189 --> 00:03:22.978
Step nine:

00:03:23.238 --> 00:03:24.498
attach the extension.

00:03:25.196 --> 00:03:29.458
Lay it along the isolated natural lash, in the same direction as the lash.

00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:34.658
The base of the extension sits about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin,

00:03:34.925 --> 00:03:36.178
never touching the skin.

00:03:36.668 --> 00:03:40.258
Press it gently, so it lies snugly along the natural lash.

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:45.321
Hold still for a moment so the glue grabs, then release the curved tweezers,

00:03:45.271 --> 00:03:46.338
and last of all,

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.858
the isolation tweezers.

00:03:48.415 --> 00:03:49.477
An important tip:

00:03:49.825 --> 00:03:54.117
never attach lashes that sit right next to each other, one after another.

00:03:54.539 --> 00:03:57.646
Attach one at the outer corner, then one in the middle,

00:03:57.596 --> 00:04:00.037
then one at the inner corner, then go back.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:03.914
That way, the glue on the previous lash has time to cure,

00:04:03.864 --> 00:04:06.597
and neighboring lashes do not stick together.

00:04:06.964 --> 00:04:11.397
Many technicians also alternate between the eyes, so each side gets a rest.

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:12.833
Step ten:

00:04:13.088 --> 00:04:14.113
check for stickies.

00:04:14.439 --> 00:04:18.780
After each zone, glide the straight tweezers lightly through the lashes,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:19.793
from base to tip:

00:04:20.062 --> 00:04:21.953
every lash must stand on its own.

00:04:22.217 --> 00:04:26.913
If you find two lashes stuck together, separate them right away, very gently.

00:04:27.261 --> 00:04:29.672
Miss one sticky, and the client will feel it,

00:04:29.622 --> 00:04:32.033
and the natural lash gets pulled as it grows.

00:04:32.704 --> 00:04:34.914
For length, the basic rule is:

00:04:35.021 --> 00:04:36.644
shortest in the inner corner,

00:04:36.594 --> 00:04:39.954
then gradually longer toward the middle and the outer corner,

00:04:39.984 --> 00:04:42.194
for a soft, natural eye shape.

00:04:42.852 --> 00:04:47.815
At the inner corner, the natural lashes are short and fine, so choose short,

00:04:47.765 --> 00:04:48.914
light extensions.

00:04:49.423 --> 00:04:51.360
Choosing a style for each eye shape,

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.034
we will learn in detail in the lash mapping lesson.

00:04:54.672 --> 00:04:55.475
Step eleven:

00:04:55.727 --> 00:04:56.435
finishing.

00:04:57.023 --> 00:05:00.115
Brush the lashes again, then compare both eyes:

00:05:00.421 --> 00:05:04.275
length, fullness and curl must be even and balanced.

00:05:04.705 --> 00:05:08.995
Remove the pads very gently, while the client's eyes are still closed.

00:05:09.495 --> 00:05:11.475
Then tell her to open her eyes slowly.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:16.035
If her eyes sting or water, let her close them again and rest a moment.

00:05:16.628 --> 00:05:17.556
Step twelve:

00:05:17.662 --> 00:05:18.516
aftercare.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:24.007
No water, no steam, no swimming, for as long as the glue maker advises,

00:05:23.957 --> 00:05:25.716
usually 24 to 48 hours.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:30.356
No oil based products at the lash base, because oil weakens the glue.

00:05:30.969 --> 00:05:34.116
Brush the lashes gently every day with a clean wand.

00:05:34.386 --> 00:05:37.236
No rubbing, no pulling, no lash curler.

00:05:37.585 --> 00:05:40.756
And book the refill right away, for two to three weeks later.

00:05:41.375 --> 00:05:42.834
Once the client has gone:

00:05:42.936 --> 00:05:47.234
used lash wands, cotton swabs and pads go into a lidded bin.

00:05:47.823 --> 00:05:50.832
Tweezers are cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:53.634
as in the lesson on handling tools after each client.

00:05:54.136 --> 00:05:56.114
Wipe down the bed and the work table.

00:05:56.369 --> 00:05:58.994
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
